strategies.objective:
Put all four candidate gold-free faithfulness metrics in play on the same real NL→FOL outputs, and pick the one (or complementary pair) that deserves iter 2's depth under a rule fixed before any scores exist. The four are:
- (i) the monotonicity/role signature: absolute, relativized, and zero-LLM text-side variants;
- (ii) solver-chosen truth-value-judgment worlds;
- (iii) prover-derived instance consequences checked by small NLI;
- (iv) latent-class estimation across systems.
In the same iteration, build the independently labelled held-out meta-evaluation set on which the survivor is confirmed. That set uses 6 current systems and 3 corpora, with adjudicated labels that estimate the correct-but-inequivalent and wrong-gold rates, plus the real error-type mix. The contribution being built toward: the first gold-free NL→FOL metric shown to add signal over LLM-judge and round-trip baselines on real outputs, especially on long, heavily conditioned sentences, with its blind spots predicted in advance.

strategies.rationale:
DIAGNOSIS OF ITER 1.
(1) Cross-system latent class (LC_onecoin) was the only rule survivor: AUROC .853 and G3 +.111. But its labels and its clustering share the same bijection-equivalence checker. Under Arm A's labels it fell to .772, and 44% of 'non-equivalent' candidates are actually faithful. Its win may therefore be partly 'agrees with gold's vocabulary'. Only the held-out panel labels can settle this, and the rule pre-registered in iter 1 requires confirmation there.
(2) TVJT failed only G2. Its false alarms appear even on pure REORDER (.42) and DEMORGAN (.35) rewrites, which cannot change meaning. So the failure is instrument noise: syntax-dependent mutant and world selection plus gemini non-determinism. It is not a semantic defect, and it is repairable by construction. TVJT is also the only metric whose AUROC ROSE with complexity (top tercile .751 vs B1 .552, delta +.20 [.09, .31]). That is exactly the crossover the hypothesis predicted and the user's stated priority.
(3) The signature (A1 .711, A3 zero-LLM .718) added +.09 over judge+parse. But much of that came from alignment coverage (A0 .674): polarity added no significant increment beyond it. It failed G2 only through SYN_RENAME alignment (38-42%; logical rewrites 0/270). The text side is the bottleneck (LLM probe downward accuracy on MED .60; rule marker .86), and every metric sat at chance in the top tercile. Pushing its AUROC harder would be the 'shrink to fit' move this pipeline forbids.

SIDEWAYS MOVE FOR THE SIGNATURE. Its unique, lead-able properties are:
- it NAMES the error type at zero LLM cost, and real errors are dominated by added/dropped condition (39%) and forall/exists (22%), the types it sees by construction;
- it can be run text-vs-GOLD to flag wrong gold without any reference (for example, ProverQA golds that drop restrictors such as 'For all fish');
- its blind spots were predicted in advance.
These claims can come out positive even if its ranking AUROC stays modest, and each answers a user requirement directly: error-type naming and wrong-gold handling.

WHY THIS SHAPE. This is the final iteration, and the candidate population was already screened in iter 1, so this is a DEEP TEST and CONFIRMATION iteration, not another wide screen. There are three slots, each a distinct piece a reviewer needs:
- slot 1 is the frozen, pre-registered held-out confirmation plus the full baseline panel and system-level analysis (the table the paper must have);
- slot 2 is the mechanism-level deep test of the crossover, the user's highest-priority regime, with the instrument repaired;
- slot 3 turns the main hypothesis into its diagnostic and gold-audit contribution.
All three read the same held-out item_ids and labels from art_iyzYyaqlqpSX and compute the same fixed-prompt cheap judge (B1). Their per-item scores therefore join into one table in the report. Zero-LLM components (LC, A3) are recomputed in every artifact that needs them for stacking, so no artifact waits on another.

PRE-REGISTERED CONFIRMATION CRITERIA, fixed now and copied into every artifact. Primary population: the 609 panel3 held-out items, with post-stratified weights (metadata_L3_design_weight / L3_poststratum). Weighted AUROC uses a 1000x bootstrap clustered by sentence and stratified by design stratum. A metric is CONFIRMED iff:
- (C1) weighted AUROC >= 0.70;
- (C2) delta-AUROC of the cross-fitted logistic [B1 + parse_ok + best other baselines + metric] over the same model without the metric has a 95% lower bound > 0;
- (C3) coverage >= 70%, with unscored items set to 0.5 and kept in.
The CROSSOVER is confirmed iff the metric-minus-B1 AUROC gap has a positive, CI-excluding-0 slope across complexity terciles (a logistic interaction test on panel items plus top-tercile audited-solver items) AND the top-tercile gap has a lower bound > 0. Every result is reported under panel labels (primary) and audited-solver labels (secondary). If LC confirms only under solver labels, it is reported as 'agrees with gold vocabulary', not as faithfulness.
